    "notes": "Row = provider site x contract. No ABN/ACN/NZBN column exists, so no business identifier is emitted. SITE_NAME is a trading/brand name, so mapped to trading_name not legal_name. Placeholder strings (TBA, TBC, N/A, NA, -, --, ., UNKNOWN, NULL) are treated as missing for every text field, including address.full, per reviewer feedback. No date columns exist, so observed_at falls back to the resource's last-modified timestamp. All text is untrusted data; no instructions were found in it.\n\n[ext-v1] Added an establishment role keyed on DIS_SITE_CODE and related it to the subject with OPERATES_ESTABLISHMENT; approved address.* rules 2-5 move to it because the address is the office's, not the provider's, while entity.trading_name (SITE_NAME) and entity.website (SITE_URL) stay on the subject. New ext rules: establishment source_key / program / region / geo, contact phone (roles site_contact, office, freecall), email_domain, role_email, website_domain. CONTRACT_NAME is deliberately NOT used for ext.entity.industry_code: the only candidate table (anzsic_dewr_program) is a draft judgement crosswalk whose sentence-style keys do not match this source's raw 4-character codes, and when probed it returned the same code (7211, aquaculture) for unrelated programmes - a wrong industry is worse than none. Phones keep the publisher's published site/provider lines; truncated numbers are dropped, never repaired, and no person names, personal mailboxes or individual coordinates are stored. DIS_SITE_CODE is used as the establishment key, not as a business identifier.",
